de Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T13:30:15-08:00","id":1362713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1361844#post1361844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Look, it\u2019s not my fault the alleged difference between \u201csentience\u201d and \u201csapience\u201d changes every time someone insists there is one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Subscribe to the comparative cognition newsletter and get mad at people for using either one of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T14:17:06-08:00","id":1362729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1362690#post1362690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forum ate my post.<br /> <br /> FOR FUCK'S SAKE!!!<br /> <br /> Short version: I've heard the arguments of ace people who find the Red Rule unsatisfying because they feel it still says they have sexual feelings that they inform us they do not have in the least. I wish to respect the distinction and promote others to do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having seen that argument on rpg.net (seen it kill the thread it was in, at that), that's a large part of why my take on RLSS is the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T15:42:35-08:00","id":1362744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1362729#post1362729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having seen that argument on rpg.net (seen it kill the thread it was in, at that), that's a large part of why my take on RLSS is the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back over your statement, I feel a bit wary of that, but don't want to presume to speak for asexual people being suggesting a careful approach.<br /> <br /> For my own perspective, I would prefer to focus the Charm on the sexual dynamic because I think it has intriguing layers of interpersonal relationship that can be handled with maturity. Even framed in terms of lust... maybe it's just because it's often loaded, but I think it's a small word for what can make people want each other even when not romantic.<br /> <br /> Intimacies can already be there to handle when the sex is more... let's say transactional. I would not personally care for that as the avenue through which Rose-Lipped Seduction Style works.<br /> <br /> ... At least not in its own. I suppose I'm still seeing how a character might have no such Intimacies, but the natural dynamic between them and the Solar is still a bit more businesslike.<br /> <br /> That also feels very natural as one of the dynamics along which a Solar initiates relations with a non-human being of great power.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm thinking back on my recent observations of how the relationships that the famed Cleopatra had with Julius Caesar and Marc Antony were so distinct in history. Sure, monarchs (or close enough) of different states have relationships, but rarely with quite that kind of... personal closeness and pageantry and drama so deeply intertwined with the political elements. Nevermind that both Caesar and Antony were married men at the time, and all the cultural hangups about things like obvious extramarital affairs and such relations with a non-Roman.<br /> <br /> Certainly, the part about Caesar including a golden idol to Cleopatra in his family shrine feels very much like something an Exalt might do for their godly lover that entails a touch of scandal in both their worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T17:12:11-08:00","id":1362760,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> It's probably an environmental difference. <br /> I play all my games in a left-leaning open-table environment. At any point in time, I could have a new player join and that player is fairly likely to be or closely associate with somebody who is LGBT and therefore who may feel strongly about RLSS's implications. For that reason, I feel obligated to make sure I don't run any risk of offending anyone by leaving that landmine armed. <br /> If you have a closed group where you know nobody will be offended by RLSS's implications, then of course you don't need to worry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T17:15:25-08:00","id":1362762,"title":"","content":"I very recently read in more detail than I had before about the life of Madame du Pompadour, and thinking about how that might relate to this subject got me considering an angle that is maybe not so often thought of in Exalted or stories in general.<br /> <br /> Set the scene; a Solar poet and shipwright of the West, and the nymph elemental who has been his extended contact with the local ocean spirit court. The two have gotten to know each other very well, in addition to the physical attraction.<br /> <br /> Solar: In all the time I've known you've brought me feelings of solace and trust and understanding I never thought possible. I love you!<br /> Nymph: I'm so happy to hear those words. The wonders that you have wrought, the beauty of the words and verse with which you have painted myself and the sea, and your humility, earnestness and care have captured my heart. Take me in your arms!<br /> {the two lock in a passionate embrace, fading tastefully to black. Cut back to them lying in bed staring at the ceiling with looks of wonder on their face}<br /> Solar: Wow. That was just {expression falls a bit} awful.<br /> Nymph: Oh thank the Voice you said it, I didn't know what to do.<br /> Solar: Somewhere between the texture of your whalebone teeth, the webbing on your digits and the viscosity of your body, I just did not enjoy that at all.<br /> Nymph: Yeah, being able to tell the entire time took a lot of the fun out of it for me as well. And if I'm being perfectly honest, I wasn't really fond of what you were doing with your hands.<br /> Solar: Then there was that moment when you softened up a bit and I kind of... sank into you...<br /> {both shudder at the memory}<br /> Nymph: Do you think of we tried again we might work something out?<br /> Solar: I'd really really prefer not to.<br /> Nymph: Yeah, good call.<br /> {they lie in silence for a few moments}<br /> Nymph: What do we do now?<br /> Solar: I'm not sure. I mean, I still totally adore you and think of you as my best friend and my muse.<br /> Nymph: And I still admire your strength of character and artistic spirit and want to support you for the rest of your days.<br /> Solar: Sooo... do you want to live together as husband and wife and get our sexual gratification through meaningless trysts with other people?<br /> Nymph: Sounds good to me.<br /> {they high five, still not quite ready to look at one another}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T17:29:56-08:00","id":1362763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1362760#post1362760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that player is fairly likely to be or closely associate with somebody who is LGBT and therefore who may feel strongly about RLSS's implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are... a few implications one can take from Rose-Lipped Seduction Style as it intersects with sexuality in particular. My perspective on one of the more harmonious would be to focus on the instances in reality in which heterosexual or homosexual people have had relations with somebody they wouldn't normally be attracted to on grounds that their appearance and/or character were compelling enough to be provocative and make them curious about exploring the range of their sexuality, and to say that it's possible for a Solar Exalt to empower those qualities within themselves.<br /> <br /> Within the limits of the Red Rule. &quot;Sure I'm flattered, maybe even a little curious, but the answer is no.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I'm just throwing my perspective into the mix of the conversation, I certainly don't want to disregard anybody's boundaries. Honestly I feel a bit over the line with what I've said so far. I think I'll let it rest for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:50:08-08:00","id":1363089,"title":"","content":"This is certainly my prefered application of the last line of Rose-Lipped Seduction Style.<br /> <br /> Not Cthulhu specifically, but something that the Storyteller's created to be a monster rather than a character and certainly they're being engaged with in a way they didn't intend but is nevertheless interesting. It's applications vs. humans are creepy and begging to be shut down by the red rule.<br /> <br /> The only possible role I can see it playing would've been better served by Storytelling advice. While &quot;everyone is bisexual&quot; became a grating meme the sexual orientation of a newly introduced NPC, especially a no-name one like &quot;jailor with keys jangling from his belt&quot; or &quot;young noble woman&quot; should probably be pretty fluidic out of respect for cooperative storytelling and character engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:37:47-08:00","id":1363102,"title":"","content":"I personally kind of assume that the primary application of that function is being able to go straight to attempting seduction on people with compatible orientation without first establishing an Intimacy to you in them.<br /> <br /> Which doeeessss raise a question about how it interacts with Decision Points. It's not even like the Lunar Charms, it doesn't state that the persuade attempt functions as though the person has even a minor Intimacy the necessary purposes. And it's quite clear on how it's supplementing a persuade action, Decision Points have to come into play at some point.<br /> <br /> So I think there are valid grounds for even Minor Intimacies that might be read as contrary to going along with it to serve for saying &quot;no dice&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not proposing that would be sufficient for people who find the Charm's premise on the whole to be objectionable, just a detail worth including in <b>anybody's</b> assessment of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:29:06-08:00","id":1363195,"title":"","content":"Personally I see the interaction with orientation as a valuable player tool. If seduction is a big enough part of your character\u2019s shtick to have an Essence 3 Charm for it it could arguably become a bit of a buzzkill for near-half of everyone to be categorically immune like they otherwise would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 01-24-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:44:29-08:00","id":1363199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363195#post1363195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I see the interaction with orientation as a valuable player tool. If seduction is a big enough part of your character\u2019s shtick to have an Essence 3 Charm for it it could arguably become a bit of a buzzkill for near-half of everyone to be categorically immune like they otherwise would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it just seems for an Ess 3 charm the effect of \u201cbe even more attractive to someone who would find you attractive in a bar anyway\u201d to be kind of (extremely) anemic.<br /> <br /> If I were to run it (based on discussions in the Discord about dev intent), I would say it would run like so:<br /> <br /> 1. Golem of Prague, a Mountain etc: Definitely Okay.<br /> <br /> 2. Cthulhu, Neverborn, Unformed Wyld Entities: Definitely Okay.<br /> <br /> 3. Issues regarding orientation and preference: You discuss this with your ST and group and do what is most beneficial for the whole dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-24-2020, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T15:35:19-08:00","id":1363207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363195#post1363195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I see the interaction with orientation as a valuable player tool. If seduction is a big enough part of your character\u2019s shtick to have an Essence 3 Charm for it it could arguably become a bit of a buzzkill for near-half of everyone to be categorically immune like they otherwise would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363199#post1363199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it just seems for an Ess 3 charm the effect of \u201cbe even more attractive to someone who would find you attractive in a bar anyway\u201d to be kind of (extremely) anemic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so I'm clear, you both are referring specifically to matters of sexuality in these points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T15:42:20-08:00","id":1363208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363207#post1363207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Just so I'm clear, you both are referring specifically to matters of sexuality in these points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as concerns the ability to seduce creatures from beyond the comprehension of man and who blot out the horizon with their bottomless orifices, yes?<br /> <br /> Red Rule and Orichalcum Rule permitting of course.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T20:08:36-08:00","id":1363238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363195#post1363195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I see the interaction with orientation as a valuable player tool. If seduction is a big enough part of your character\u2019s shtick to have an Essence 3 Charm for it it could arguably become a bit of a buzzkill for near-half of everyone to be categorically immune like they otherwise would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it's a poor substitute for good storytelling advice. Over the last decade or so most &quot;seducer characters&quot; I've seen have a couple of instances of incompatible orientation in the entire chronicle, mostly because the Storyteller world built around the idea that the characters were socially aware enough to not be constantly barking up the wrong tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T01:05:05-08:00","id":1363264,"title":"","content":"Honestly not sure what you\u2019re trying to say there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T05:46:47-08:00","id":1363283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363264#post1363264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly not sure what you\u2019re trying to say there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she's saying:<br /> <br /> Think of an old James Bond film. Every villian always has an attractive, heterosexual female deputy for Bond to seduce. Bond never has to try to seduce a straight man. Bond's seduction attempts never fail because the female deputy is a lesbian.<br /> <br /> The fictional world of James Bond might contain straight men and lesbians (and ugly women), but as a storytelling conciet, these people are never in positions where Bond has to seduce them. Ever.<br /> <br /> If the story demands Bond seduce someone, that someone is always a straight, attractive, woman who is open to his advances.<br /> <br /> Ergo Bond doesn't need the ability to seduce straight men or Cthulu. Because the director/screen writers/storyteller will never put him in that position.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> You are now picturing Gert Fr\u00f6be demonstrating to Sean Connory why they <i>really</i> call him &quot;Goldfinger&quot;. You are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-25-2020, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T18:13:05-08:00","id":1363377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363283#post1363283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are now picturing Gert Fr\u00f6be demonstrating to Sean Connory why they <i>really</i> call him &quot;Goldfinger&quot;. You are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P_SlAzsXa7E\" target=\"_blank\">I am not and I don't need to.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:15:45-08:00","id":1363470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363283#post1363283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think she's saying:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's partially it, but also-<br /> <br /> The Storyteller controls every aspect of the game world including what the players see and to this end they supply what I call &quot;passive competence&quot; where they supply enough information for the players actions to not be frustrating guessing games.<br /> <br /> To me the potential &quot;buzzkill&quot; of a James Bond expy hitting on a lesbian and getting turned down isn't infringing on an intrinsic right to fuck every attractive woman but that the Storyteller doesn't attribute them much passive competence in this area, so he has no indication of her sexual orientation until she invokes it to shut him down like he's a pickup artist who hangs around bars in James Bond cosplay. If he's really a master of seduction he should probably notice the lack of interest from her really early on and realise he needs a different strategy rather than bypassing her sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if the hypothetical Storyteller doesn't care about the character\u2019s shtick or the possible buzzkill from being turned down, then using Rose-Lipped Seduction Style to brute force the issue is taking a gamble that they won't go onto portray the character as a rapist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-26-2020, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T12:38:55-08:00","id":1363496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1361110#post1361110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, all I can think of when I read that title was &quot;I didn't know Chuck Tingle was an Exalted fan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is...rather plausible, really.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lets face it - most chuck tingle book titles sound like Exalted ERP plothooks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T16:00:40-08:00","id":1363696,"title":"","content":"Lioness's points add to my feeling that practically speaking the Charm might be primarily used to empower a particular kind of persuade action without being required to build up the necessary Intimacy beforehand. That might be how it ought to be.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't think that renders the Charm anemic, because setting aside the matter of whether compatible sexuality automatically equates to being specifically attracted to a given person, there's still a social system with rules.<br /> <br /> For the matter of sexuality, I'm starting to think that kind of thing mostly belongs in a sustained story in which a continuous cast of characters with established traits is interacted with, and some complicated relationship shenanigans are on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-27-2020, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T18:44:10-08:00","id":1363715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361102-don-t-f-k-the-gay-f-k-cthulhu?p=1363696#post1363696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lioness's points add to my feeling that practically speaking the Charm might be primarily used to empower a particular kind of persuade action without being required to build up the necessary Intimacy beforehand. That might be how it ought to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Essence 1 Performance Charm already does that and then some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T05:09:29-08:00","id":1363774,"title":"","content":"I don't feel capable of assessing the relative values of differing mote costs and the other things both Charms can do, including the distinction between the specific wordings of &quot;doesn't need an Intimacy&quot; and &quot;can achieve otherwise unacceptable influence&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do think that a position of placing specific value in the capacity to persuade in spite of sexuality needs to at least be handled carefully by a player pursuing it. That's not to say don't do it, just do it with consideration.<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure what to make of the statement about &quot;it won't work on half of all people&quot;. <br /> <br /> I think this is beginning to veer into a problem area for me (in terms of my current standards for my own conduct), so I intend to leave my thoughts on the subject at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T05:24:16-08:00","id":1363776,"title":"","content":"When I said before about the possibility that humans might be engaging partners for things like the quality of their erogenous zones, I was initially thinking in comparison to things like those tentacle monsters the Jadeborn fight so much, but then I thought about the Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> I can't recall the topic of things like mating or families ever being described in text for them before. As the latter goes, it seems to me that they have basically no concept of blood kinship or lineage; I think their eggs are supposed to be hatched in communal creches, and with the whole thing that they regard you primarily as the continuation of a single soul and the relationships of its past lives are what matter, biological relatives seem kind of irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Heck, I think gender might be a bit irrelevant to them socially, most of the time.<br /> <br /> And with their population always having been limited to a specific number, it makes reproduction feel like the kind of thing that might be at risk of being fruitless. I don't think there was ever a reference suggesting that eggs only ever get fertilised if there are definitely souls available.<br /> <br /> It makes me picture a scenario in which Dragon Kings don't have much in the way of a sex drive or sexual passions, and are on a reproductive cycle on the order of every few years they mate in order to produce sufficient clutches of eggs to accommodate all of the souls that have been referred houseless since the last time.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking this because I do like generally playing up some of the low key alien qualities of the Dragon Kings. That and thinking it's a little fun to imagine that spirits and the like wouldn't have generally card to sleep with them.<br /> <br /> I'm not looking back over my books describing them right now, so I don't know if there's any more in depth description of their biology or references to grand romances that I've overlooked. Mind, even the latter could be the kind of thing that could be reconciled with an assumption that they're beings with little interest in sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}